  "facts": [
    "The Meridian Highway Bridge, completed in 1924, was the last link of the Meridian Highway, now U.S. Route 81, and opened as a toll bridge on October 11, 1924.",
    "Designed with a movable span for river traffic, the bridge never saw trains on its lower level, yet it carried northbound cars on the top deck and southbound on the bottom after 1953.",
    "After a 2008 inspection revealed corrosion, a 10‑ton weight limit was imposed until the Discovery Bridge opened on October 11, 2008, exactly 84 years after the Meridian Bridge’s dedication."
